---
import UseCaseLayout from "../../layouts/UseCaseLayout.astro";
import { TECH_DEBT, aiExposure, sensitiveData } from "../../data/page-answers.ts";
---

<UseCaseLayout
  title="Is Your Salesforce Org Ready for AI Agents? Audit It"
  description="Before you switch on Agentforce or another AI agent, check what it could reach: sensitive fields, broad permissions, guest access, old automation and debt."
  path="/use-cases/agent-readiness-audit"
  heading="Is the org ready for AI agents?"
  lede="An AI agent inherits the org it runs in: every broad permission, every sensitive field it can reach, every forgotten flow. Check those first, from the metadata, without giving anything new access."
  crumb="Agent readiness"
  audience="architects, security reviewers and admins planning Agentforce"
  short="Ask your AI assistant a short series of questions: which fields look sensitive, what your agents can reach, who has broad access, what’s exposed to guest users, and how much technical debt there is. sf-intelligence answers each from your org’s metadata, offline, and says plainly what each check couldn’t see."
  answers={[sensitiveData, aiExposure]}
  answerIntro="Two of the checks, run on Verdant, the demo org."
  asks={[
    "Which fields look like they hold sensitive data?",
    "What can our AI agents reach?",
    "Who has View All Data or Modify All Data?",
    "What can guest users see?",
    "Score the technical debt in this org.",
    "Which custom fields does nothing use?",
  ]}
  checks={[
    "<strong>Sensitive fields</strong>, flagged by name, type and description",
    "<strong>Agent setup</strong>: topics, actions and prompt templates, and the fields they touch",
    "<strong>Broad permissions</strong> and permission sets nobody seems to need",
    "<strong>Guest and Experience Cloud exposure</strong>, when your refresh pulled it",
    "<strong>Technical debt</strong>: old automation, Apex risks, unused fields and classes",
  ]}
  limits={[
    "What an agent actually did at run time. This reads configuration",
    "Personal data stored in fields with unremarkable names",
    "Record-level data, unless you turn on the optional live mode",
    "Areas your refresh didn’t pull. They are left out of scores, not counted as clean",
  ]}
  tools={["pii_inventory", "ai_exposure_report", "guest_exposure_report", "permission_risk_report", "tech_debt_score", "unused_fields_deep", "org_risk_report"]}
  related={[
    { href: "/ai-safety", label: "Is AI safe on my Salesforce org?" },
    { href: "/use-cases/sharing-troubleshooting", label: "Sharing and access", note: "use case" },
    { href: "/compare/hubbl", label: "sf-intelligence vs Hubbl", note: "if you need a scored audit report" },
    { href: "/trust", label: "Trust and security" },
  ]}
  faqs={[
    {
      q: "Does the audit give the agent any access?",
      a: "No. The checks read your metadata snapshot on your computer. Nothing is installed in the org and nothing is granted.",
    },
    {
      q: "Is the sensitive-data check a compliance scan?",
      a: "No. It flags fields by their names, types and descriptions, never their values. Treat it as a starting list for a review, and expect it to miss fields with unremarkable names.",
    },
    {
      q: "How is the debt score worked out?",
      a: "It weighs several areas, such as unused metadata, legacy automation, Apex quality and old API versions. Areas it couldn’t check are left out of the score and named, so a low score on a partial snapshot isn’t passed off as a clean bill.",
    },
  ]}
  cta={{ question: sensitiveData.question, related: { href: "/ai-safety", label: "Is AI safe on my org?" } }}
  dateModified="2026-10-10"
>
  <h2>A score that says what it skipped</h2>
  <p>On the demo org the technical debt score comes out at {TECH_DEBT.score} out of 100 ({TECH_DEBT.band}; higher is worse). The answer also says only {TECH_DEBT.scoredAreas} of {TECH_DEBT.totalAreas} areas could be scored, because the refresh didn’t pull everything the others need. A score with its gaps named is more useful than a confident number built on missing data.</p>
  <h2>Order the checks by risk</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>What could the agent see?</strong> Sensitive fields, and the agent’s own actions and context.</li>
    <li><strong>Who else can see it?</strong> Broad permissions, guest access and sharing.</li>
    <li><strong>What would it act on?</strong> Old automation, unused fields and code with known risks.</li>
  </ol>
</UseCaseLayout>
